From: John Törnblom <john.tornblom@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glsl: find the glslang libraries in -Dvulkan-sdk

Only SPIRV and the static helper libraries were looked up in
<vulkan-sdk>/lib; glslang and glslang-default-resource-limits were looked
up in the compiler's search directories only. When those don't include the
directory glslang is installed in (the PS4 toolchain reports only
<sysroot>/lib, not <sysroot>/usr/lib), SPIRV is found but glslang is
silently left out, and the final link fails.

---
diff --git a/src/glsl/meson.build b/src/glsl/meson.build
index c9a8542..26f2c33 100644
--- a/src/glsl/meson.build
+++ b/src/glsl/meson.build
@@ -30,7 +30,8 @@ if glslang_req.auto() and shaderc.found()
 elif not glslang_req.disabled()
 
   glslang_deps = [
-    cxx.find_library('glslang-default-resource-limits', required: false)
+    cxx.find_library('glslang-default-resource-limits', required: false,
+                     dirs: get_option('vulkan-sdk') != '' ? [get_option('vulkan-sdk') / 'lib'] : [])
   ]
 
   # meson doesn't respect generator expressions in INTERFACE_LINK_LIBRARIES
@@ -59,7 +60,7 @@ elif not glslang_req.disabled()
 
     # Glslang 15.0.0 moved some code around, add also linking to glslang, while
     # this is not needed for older versions, it will still work.
-    glslang_deps += cxx.find_library('glslang', required: required, static: static)
+    glslang_deps += cxx.find_library('glslang', required: required, static: static, dirs: vulkan_lib_dirs)
 
     if static
       glslang_deps += [
